# back/bow: the fighter's bow slung on the back out of combat (`sheath bowback`: P2C_CONTRACTS 3, decision D6), P2c
# SLICE-ARMS 2026-10-23: the self bow from the left shoulder to the right hip (the stave and string as the hunter's carried
# bow, held/civil/bow, so the two read as one bow), crossing the quiver's strap. Sheath channel: rest, kick, lag, sit,
# stride; drawn and lie draw nothing (the bow is in the left hand: held/weapons/bow_self; or under the body). Format: doll.h.
use person
legend V linen 0
legend W linen 1
legend X linen 2
legend Y linen 3
legend Z linen 4
body adult
role sheath bowback
anchor neck
keys sheath
z 30

